                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9d75320f-d81d-4e9c-8753-026780499a83",
                        "entry_id": "522674b2-8416-37df-8f4c-e3673094f577",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mossies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f179f24e-f8d4-3fb3-8438-8758ae8ec1f9",
                        "entry_id": "522674b2-8416-37df-8f4c-e3673094f577",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of various species of sparrow, especially Passer melanurus."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "South-Africa"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8838ae46-fbfd-4ea1-8bd4-3df40630e738",
                                "sense_id": "f179f24e-f8d4-3fb3-8438-8758ae8ec1f9",
                                "text": "Our four baby mossies have left the nest."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c66b394-ba65-4639-a197-60988b45c2cd",
                                "sense_id": "f179f24e-f8d4-3fb3-8438-8758ae8ec1f9",
                                "text": "Another highly successful species, which has become a serious pest of fruit, is the Mossie or Cape Sparrow. The male mossie, with his black and white head and rufous mantle, is rather a handsome little bird; his wife lacks the head markings, being grey-brown with a pale eye-stripe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f516604-1b30-40f0-9ba8-d933ee9a8834",
                                "sense_id": "f179f24e-f8d4-3fb3-8438-8758ae8ec1f9",
                                "text": "He laughs a deep laugh that rumbles up from somewhere in his drumskin stomach. It spooks the mossies on the overhead telegraph wire."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "2eb22063-b6fe-3714-8f73-83eb44dd0839",
                "word": "mossie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b3dd25c2-9bea-425c-a33d-7d2c26a5d930",
                        "entry_id": "2eb22063-b6fe-3714-8f73-83eb44dd0839",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mossies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b1a266a5-3ac2-318d-8004-286c1547e2c8",
                        "entry_id": "2eb22063-b6fe-3714-8f73-83eb44dd0839",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A mosquito."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "New-Zealand",
                            "UK",
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb783b35-2485-4a32-9f27-ec79b633cba6",
                                "sense_id": "b1a266a5-3ac2-318d-8004-286c1547e2c8",
                                "text": "She came out, standing a head taller than him, tugging a loose cotton shift into place, and made for a rough brick fireplace beside a pile of rusting pots and pans.\n‘Come inside,’ Willi said. ‘The mossies will eat you alive out here.’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "972fbfa4-0ed8-4627-bf4f-96c96b2f999d",
                                "sense_id": "b1a266a5-3ac2-318d-8004-286c1547e2c8",
                                "text": "Tip 1 : Make sure there is clearance between your body and the net. If the net touches your skin, the mossie will be able to bite you through it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e305f53-19c7-4a3f-bf47-7bdb1341df00",
                                "sense_id": "b1a266a5-3ac2-318d-8004-286c1547e2c8",
                                "text": "He had becoms full of Bay intelligence about mosquito repellent measures. Apart from the obvious—mossie coils, citronella candles, zappers, fine nets suspended over beds and Rid roll-on or spray—he decided to invest in bush gear from an army disposal store. The mossies, who know a city slicker when they bite one, had been stinging clear through his Calvin Clone T-shirts from the Hong Kong markets and feasting on his bare arms as if presented with a juicy buffet."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "3da6343f-6b6f-396b-a3a4-f22eb4065bb9",
                "word": "Mossie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "daf3f9a5-d66b-4c7f-b3f6-d4d4f0d89616",
                        "entry_id": "3da6343f-6b6f-396b-a3a4-f22eb4065bb9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Mossies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2af8b66c-5ab6-3bf4-b8ba-a0dac7a617aa",
                        "entry_id": "3da6343f-6b6f-396b-a3a4-f22eb4065bb9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A de Havilland Mosquito."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "colloquial",
                            "dated",
                            "historical",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "edaedc4a-d015-4de2-8a32-b3f321d11909",
                                "sense_id": "2af8b66c-5ab6-3bf4-b8ba-a0dac7a617aa",
                                "text": "He leaned into the electric gunsight, aiming the Mossie at the left wingroot between engine and fuselage, where he knew there were fuel tanks — his right thumb mashed the control-column firing button."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "afbd348a-e297-4826-82bd-f2813f9191af",
                                "sense_id": "2af8b66c-5ab6-3bf4-b8ba-a0dac7a617aa",
                                "text": "The Mossies were still able to land before the bombers were over the Channel."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a1d163c-2c1f-4a28-9e00-cc9f3b4e90de",
                                "sense_id": "2af8b66c-5ab6-3bf4-b8ba-a0dac7a617aa",
                                "text": "Almost 8,000 Mossies were built in Great Britain, Canada and Australia."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
